# PAM stack for intentionality-resume-gate.service's PAMName=.
#
# Its one job is pam_systemd: registering a logind session on tty9 for the
# unit's User=. Without a session, nothing running as that user may open the
# GPU or the input devices, so a compositor (cage) cannot start there and the
# graphical gate falls back to the text one. The session is on the VT the unit
# has already switched to, so logind makes it the active one and hands the
# devices over; switching back pauses it again, exactly as it does for GNOME.
#
# systemd never runs the auth stack for PAMName= (account + session only), so
# nothing here can ask for a password, and nothing here grants any.
#
# Install: sudo cp to /etc/pam.d/intentionality-gate
account  required  pam_permit.so
session  required  pam_systemd.so
